@VisRen
$Visual File Renamer (VisRen)

VisRen is F4's native visual batch renamer. It builds every new name
before anything is changed and shows source and destination names
side by side.
It works with files and directories on a local file-system panel.

If panel items are marked, VisRen opens them in panel order. If no
items are marked, it uses the item under the panel cursor. The parent
entry ".." is
never used. Open VisRen with F11 and choose "Visual File Renamer"; the
assigned menu letter can also activate it.

~Quick start and dialog fields~VisRenQuickStart@
~Name masks, extensions, ranges, counters and escapes~VisRenMasks@
~Case conversion, transliteration and processing order~VisRenTransforms@
~Dates, ID3, image/EXIF and executable metadata~VisRenMetadata@
~Search, plain replacement and regular expressions~VisRenSearch@
~Preview navigation, keyboard and mouse reference~VisRenPreview@
~Editing the rename list in the UTF-8 editor~VisRenEditor@
~Rename execution, errors, the log and Undo~VisRenRename@
~Portable filename rules and important limitations~VisRenSafety@
~Practical recipes~VisRenExamples@

The implementation follows FarPlugins VisRen 3.2.0, with stricter
filename/editor validation, stable random values and portable metadata.

@VisRenQuickStart
$VisRen: quick start and dialog fields

#A typical rename#

  1. Mark the required files/directories with Ins, or place the panel
     cursor on one item if only that item is needed.
  2. Press F11 and select VisRen.
  3. Enter masks for the name and extension. Defaults [N] and [E] keep
     both parts unchanged.
  4. Optionally enter Search for and Replace with text. Focus starts
     in Search for; Tab moves directly to Replace with.
  5. Inspect every destination. F3 shows the complete source,
     destination, or diagnostic for the current row.
  6. Choose Rename or press Enter on the default button.

#Name and Extension#

These two fields build the destination basename and extension separately.
The extension field does not include the dot. An empty extension result
removes the extension. Literal text is copied as typed; bracketed
expressions insert source text, counters, metadata or transformations.

The last dot separates the source name and extension. Thus archive.tar.gz
has name archive.tar and extension gz. README has no extension. A dotfile
such as .gitignore has an empty name and extension gitignore.

#Templates and [+]#

The Name templates and Extension templates lists contain expressions
valid for the corresponding mask. Choosing an entry only selects it.
The [+] button inserts that selected template at the caret and returns
focus to the corresponding mask, exactly like the original VisRen.
When a template list has focus, Ins inserts its current entry while
keeping focus in the list. Range and counter placeholders become usable
values when inserted.

#Search controls#

Search and replacement are applied after both masks have built one
complete filename. Case sensitive is enabled initially. Regular
expression switches between literal search and regex mode. Details are
in the Search topic.

#Live preview and diagnostics#

Every edit updates the preview. If a mask, range, counter, regex, or
resulting filename is invalid, all destinations become <Error!>.
Rename and F4 Editor are disabled. F3 shows the actual diagnostic.

The four edit fields use F4's history. Values used for Rename are added
to their histories. Word delimiters for [T] are stored separately in
the VisRen user configuration.

Press Backspace to return to the VisRen contents.

@VisRenMasks
$VisRen: masks, ranges, counters and escapes

#Basic expressions#

  [N]          Original name without the last extension.
  [E]          Original extension without its leading dot.
  [[]          A literal opening square bracket.
  []]          A literal closing square bracket.

All text outside expressions is literal. A stray closing bracket, an
unclosed opening bracket, or an unknown expression is an error.

#Ranges#

A range immediately follows N or E. Positions count Unicode characters,
not bytes, and start at 1. A negative position counts backward from
the end. The same forms work with E, for example [E1-3].

For the source name abcdefghij:

  [N2]         b                 one character
  [N2-5]       bcde              positions 2 through 5, inclusive
  [N2,5]       bcdef             five characters starting at position 2
  [N2-]        bcdefghij         position 2 through the end
  [N-2]        i                 second character from the end
  [N2--5]      bcdef             position 2 through fifth from the end
  [N-8-5]      cde               eighth-from-end through fifth-from-end
  [N-8,5]      cdefg             five chars starting eighth from the end
  [N-5-]       fghij             fifth from the end through the end

An out-of-bounds part is clipped where possible or produces an empty
result. Position zero and a reversed range are errors. The range
template from the drop-down uses the longest source name or extension.

#Counters#

  [C1]         1, 2, 3, ...
  [C001]       001, 002, 003, ...
  [C001+5]     001, 006, 011, ...
  [C10+-2]     10, 08, 06, ...

The initial digits set the first value and minimum display width. They
may contain at most nine digits. If +step is omitted, the step is 1. The
counter follows the preview order, so Ctrl+Up/Down or drag-and-drop
changes assigned values. Width is a minimum: larger values are not cut.

#Combining expressions#

Expressions and literals can be freely combined. For example,
[C001+1]_[N1-12] creates a three-digit sequence, an underscore, and the
first twelve characters of the old name. Transform expressions add no
text; they modify the part as described in the Transformations topic.

Press Backspace to return to the VisRen contents.

@VisRenTransforms
$VisRen: transformations and processing order

#Case transformations#

  [L]          Convert the entire mask result to lower case.
  [U]          Convert it to upper case.
  [F]          Upper-case the first character; lower-case the rest.
  [T]          Upper-case the first character of every word.
  [M]          Format an "Artist - title" style music name.

[T] uses the word delimiters "-. _&" by default. Select [T] in either
template list and press F4 to edit the delimiter characters. At most 18
characters are stored in the VisRen configuration and reused later.

[M] recognizes " - " or "_-_" between artist and title. Artist words are
title-cased; the title starts with one capital and otherwise becomes
lower case. The isolated Russian conjunction meaning "and" in an
artist name is
lower-cased, matching the original VisRen behavior.

If several case expressions occur in one mask, priority is fixed in this
order: [L], [U], [F], [T], [M]. Only the highest-priority one is applied.

#Transliteration#

  [TL]         Transliterate Russian Cyrillic to VisRen Latin spelling.
  [TR]         Convert that Latin spelling back to Russian Cyrillic.

The mapping is the original VisRen table: for example ё -> jo, ж -> zh,
х -> kh, щ -> shh, ю -> ju and я -> ja. Letter case is preserved where
possible. Reverse conversion chooses the longest matching Latin sequence.
If both [TL] and [TR] are present, [TL] has priority.

#Exact processing order#

  1. Name and extension expressions are expanded.
  2. The two parts are joined with a dot when the extension is non-empty.
  3. Search/Replace is applied to that complete filename.
  4. The result is split again at its last dot.
  5. Transliteration is applied to the part whose mask requested it.
  6. The selected case transformation is applied last.
  7. The final single filename component is validated.

This order matters. A case transform also affects replacement text
inserted into its part, while Search can match the generated extension.

Press Backspace to return to the VisRen contents.

@VisRenMetadata
$VisRen: dates and file metadata

Metadata is read lazily and cached once for each source item. Missing or
unsupported fields expand to an empty string and do not stop preview.

#File timestamps and session values#

  [DM]         Last-modification date in local time: YYYY.MM.DD
  [TM]         Last-modification time in local time: hh-mm-ss
  [R]          Random decimal number from 0 through 32767

[R] is assigned once when the dialog opens. It stays stable while masks
are edited and follows its source when rows are reordered. A new
VisRen session assigns new values.

#MP3 / ID3#

The track-number expression is an opening bracket, the ASCII number sign
(U+0023), and a closing bracket. The remaining expressions are:

  [t]          Track title
  [a]          Artist
  [l]          Album
  [y]          Year/date
  [g]          Genre

ID3v2.3 and ID3v2.4 frames are preferred when an ID3v2 tag exists.
Otherwise ID3v1.1 is used, including its track number and genre table.
Supported ID3 encodings include legacy system text, UTF-8 and UTF-16.

#Images and EXIF#

  [c]          JPEG EXIF camera maker
  [m]          JPEG EXIF camera model
  [d]          Capture date: YYYY.MM.DD hh-mm-ss
  [r]          Pixel dimensions as WIDTHxHEIGHT

Dimensions are available for JPEG, BMP, GIF and PNG. EXIF maker, model
and capture date are read from JPEG. If there is no usable EXIF date,
[d] uses its modification date and time. Note that lower-case [m]/[r] are
metadata, while upper-case [M]/[R] are transformation/random expressions.

#Executable version#

  [V]          Fixed file version from a Windows PE .exe or .dll resource

PE version data is parsed natively on every supported operating system. A
file with no usable fixed version expands [V] to an empty string.

Metadata text containing path separators or other forbidden filename
characters is discarded or caught by final filename validation. Always
inspect the preview when tags come from files you do not control.

Press Backspace to return to the VisRen contents.

@VisRenSearch
$VisRen: Search, Replace and regular expressions

Search/Replace runs on the complete name produced by both masks,
including the generated dot and extension. An empty Search for field
disables this
stage. Every non-overlapping match is replaced.

#Plain mode#

With Regular expression unchecked, Search for is literal text. When Case
sensitive is checked, File and file differ. When unchecked, matching
compares lower-case text; replacement is inserted exactly as typed.

Example: masks [N] and [E], Search for "draft_", and an empty Replace
value turn draft_report.txt into report.txt.

#Regular-expression mode#

Enable Regular expression for F4's Go/coregex-style engine. A pattern
can be entered directly or as /pattern/i. In slash form, write a
literal slash as \/. The optional i flag ignores case. Clearing Case
sensitive does the same. No suffix flag other than i is accepted.

Replacement references use $0 for the full match and $1 through $9 for
capturing groups. For example, on 001-report.txt:

  Search for:       /(\d+)-([^.]+)/
  Replace with:     $2-$1
  Result:           report-001.txt

A malformed pattern, unterminated /pattern/, or unsupported flag makes
the preview show <Error!>, disables Rename and Editor, and exposes the
parser diagnostic through F3.

Press Backspace to return to the VisRen contents.

Matches found in the original name are highlighted in the left preview
column. Highlighting follows Case sensitive and Regular expression,
marks every visible match and remains aligned while the column scrolls.
Text emitted by Replace with is highlighted in the right column. For a
regular expression this includes the complete expanded replacement;
an empty replacement has no visible text to highlight.

@VisRenPreview
$VisRen: preview, keyboard and mouse

The left preview column is the source; the right is the destination.
The first row is current when the dialog opens, while keyboard focus
begins in Search for. F12 moves focus to preview; from there it returns
to the Name mask.

When the list is taller than the visible preview, a vertical scrollbar
appears at its right edge. Its arrows, track and draggable thumb scroll
the list; the mouse wheel works over the preview as well. The scrollbar
disappears automatically when every row fits.

#General keys#

  F1                   Open this help.
  F2                   Toggle recording of the rename log.
  F3                   Show full names or the current error diagnostic.
  F4                   Open the list in the editor.
  F4 on [T] template   Edit title-case word delimiters.
  F5                   Maximize/restore the dialog.
  F6                   Load the available Undo operation.
  F8                   Clear the rename log after confirmation.
  F12                  Move focus to/from the preview.
  Alt+N                Focus the Name mask.
  Alt+E                Focus the Extension mask.
  Alt+S                Focus Search for.
  Alt+P                Focus Replace with.
  Alt+C                Toggle Case sensitive.
  Alt+G                Toggle Regular expression.
  Alt+T                Focus the Name template list.
  Alt+L                Focus the Extension template list.
  Enter                Activate the default Rename action.
  Esc                  Close the dialog without renaming.

#Keys while the preview has focus#

  Up/Down              Move the current row.
  Home/End             Move to the first/last row.
  PgUp/PgDn            Move by a preview page.
  Del                   Remove the row from this operation only.
  Ctrl+Up/Down          Reorder rows; counters follow the new order.
  Ctrl+Left/Right       Move the column divider.
  Ctrl+Num5             Center the divider and reset both scroll offsets.
  Alt+Left/Right        Scroll the source column horizontally.
  Left/Right            Scroll the destination column horizontally.
  Ctrl+PgUp             Close VisRen and return to the source item.

#Templates and mouse#

  Ins in a template list inserts the current template into its mask.
  Drag a preview row with the left button to reorder it.
  Right-click a preview row to show its full names/diagnostic.
  Double-left-click a row to return to that source on the panel.
  Click the zoom control in the title to maximize/restore.
  Click the Log renaming mark to toggle it; click the rest of the line
  to clear an existing log after confirmation.

Terminal resize and F5 restore an even two-column preview split.
Manual divider and horizontal-scroll changes can then be applied again.

Press Backspace to return to the VisRen contents.

@VisRenEditor
$VisRen: editing the list in the UTF-8 editor

F4 asks for the export form with explicit action buttons, then opens a
temporary UTF-8 document titled "Rename list of files" in F4's editor:

  Source + target      "source name"    "destination name"
  Targets only                          "destination name"

Every value is quoted. Quotes, backslashes and controls inside a
name use escaped string notation. Keep the surrounding quotes intact.

#Strict validation#

When the editor closes, VisRen requires:

  - exactly the same number of lines as the preview;
  - exactly one or two quoted columns, according to the chosen mode;
  - no extra text outside quoted values;
  - an unchanged source column in two-column mode;
  - one valid portable filename component for every destination.

Do not add or remove lines. In two-column mode, source identity and row
order must stay exact; only destinations may change. In one-column mode,
each destination remains tied to its source by line position. These
checks catch source changes or malformed quoting before renaming.

On error, VisRen reports the reason and offers Edit again. The editor
reopens at the offending line with your content preserved. A valid
edited
list starts sequential renaming when the editor closes. If the generated
list is byte-for-byte unchanged but contains mask changes, VisRen
asks for confirmation before using it.

Editor is disabled while preview contains <Error!> or an Undo list is
displayed.

Press Backspace to return to the VisRen contents.

@VisRenRename
$VisRen: execution, errors, log and Undo

#Sequential rename#

Rows are processed once, from top to bottom in their current order. An
unchanged name is skipped. A source that disappeared after opening the
dialog is also skipped. Files and directories use the same rules.

A destination owned by another object is never overwritten. A case-only
rename of the same object is supported, using a temporary name when
required. Other cycles are not staged: for example a -> b and b -> a
normally reaches a destination-exists error, like the original VisRen.

#Runtime errors#

Permissions, occupied/duplicate targets, platform limits and other
filesystem errors offer:

  Retry                Try the same row again.
  Skip                 Leave this source unchanged and continue.
  Skip all             Skip later errors without asking again.
  Cancel               Stop; do not process the remaining rows.

The operation is not transactional. Successful earlier renames remain in
place after Skip or Cancel. Failed and unprocessed sources stay marked
on the panel for retry. The completion message reports how many
rows succeeded.

#Rename log#

Log renaming is enabled when a new dialog opens. Its check mark means
successful pairs will be recorded in memory. F2 or the clickable mark
toggles recording. The log is not written to disk and is lost when F4
exits. It stores only the successful pairs and directory from the latest
rename operation; a trailing * on the label means a log is available.

F8, or clicking the rest of the log line, clears it after confirmation.
Running a rename while logging is disabled also leaves no Undo batch.

#Undo (F6)#

F6 loads the last batch in reverse order and shows destinations
returning to source names. The title shows the saved directory. Choose
Rename and confirm Undo, or answer No to return to normal rename mode.

Undo uses the same no-overwrite and error rules. It changes to the saved
directory before starting. The log is cleared after the attempt, even
if only part succeeds, while unresolved items remain marked.

Press Backspace to return to the VisRen contents.

@VisRenSafety
$VisRen: filename safety and limitations

Every changed destination must be one portable filename component. VisRen
rejects:

  - an empty name, "." or "..";
  - control characters (Unicode values below U+0020 or NUL);
  - <, >, :, ", *, ?, /, backslash or vertical bar;
  - a trailing space or dot;
  - DOS device basenames CON, PRN, AUX, NUL, COM1..COM9 or LPT1..LPT9,
    regardless of case or extension.

A slash cannot move an item into another directory. An unchanged
source name is allowed and simply skipped, even when that existing source
would not pass the portable rules as a newly generated name.

Preview validation catches mask syntax and portable-name errors. It
does not reserve destinations. Existing targets, duplicate results,
permissions, filesystem length limits and cycles can still produce a
runtime error. No target is overwritten.

Metadata can be absent or malformed and then expands to empty text.
Use separators carefully and always check the preview. VisRen never
creates a transaction or invents temporary names for multi-item cycles.

Press Backspace to return to the VisRen contents.

@VisRenExamples
$VisRen: practical recipes

#Number files and normalize extensions#

  Name mask:       [C001+1]_[N]
  Extension mask:  [E][L]

Produces 001_Old name.jpg, 002_Other name.jpg, and so on. Reorder the
preview first if the counter must follow a different sequence.

#Keep only a useful part of a fixed-width name#

  Source:          20260805_report_final.txt
  Name mask:       [N10-21]
  Extension mask:  [E]
  Result:          report_final.txt

#Remove a literal prefix#

  Masks:           [N] and [E]
  Search for:      draft_
  Replace with:    (empty)

#Swap regex groups#

  Source:          001-report.txt
  Search for:      /(\d+)-([^.]+)/
  Replace with:    $2-$1
  Result:          report-001.txt

#Name MP3 files from tags#

  Name mask:       [a] - [t]
  Extension mask:  [E][L]

Track-number prefixes can be made with the counter, or with the ID3 track
expression described in the Dates and metadata topic. Missing artist
or title tags expand to empty text, so inspect separators in the preview.

#Name photographs by capture time and dimensions#

  Name mask:       [d]_[r]_[C001]
  Extension mask:  [E][L]

JPEG uses EXIF capture time when present; other supported images use file
modification time for [d].

#Transliterate and add literal brackets#

  Name mask:       [[]archive[]]_[N][TL]
  Extension mask:  [E][L]

The source Пример.TXT becomes [archive]_Primer.txt with VisRen's
original transliteration table.

Press Backspace to return to the VisRen contents.

