@ViewerEditor
$Viewer & Editor Keys
This topic is generated dynamically from the action registry.

@ViewerNav
$Navigation Keys
Editor:
  Ctrl+Left     - Previous word boundary
  Ctrl+Right    - Next word boundary
  Ctrl+Shift+Left/Right - Select by words
  Home/End      - Line start / end
  PgUp/PgDn     - Page up / down

Viewer:
  Up/Down       - Scroll one line
  PgUp/PgDn     - Scroll one page
  Home/End      - File start / end

@PanelNav
$Panel Navigation
This topic is generated dynamically from the action registry.

F8 follows the "Use the trash" setting. When enabled, F4 refuses the
operation if the active file system has no recoverable trash; it never falls
back to permanent deletion. Shift+Del and Shift+NumDel always delete
permanently. Permanent removal is also available as a separate Files-menu
command and can be assigned its own hotkey.

@ApplyCmd
$Apply command (Ctrl+G)
Apply command runs a command template for marked panel entries in panel order,
or for the current entry when nothing is marked. Directories are included;
the parent row (..) is never processed. Processed marks can be restored with
Ctrl+M.

Sequential runs one command at a time. Parallel uses the selected worker
limit. Queue runs one sequential batch in the background. All modes execute
on the host that owns the active panel and provide one cancellable transcript.
Commands are noninteractive and receive closed standard input.

The transcript window can be resized or expanded with F5 and may be closed
while commands continue to run. Closing it does not cancel the batch; use
Cancel for that. Send to editor opens the currently retained transcript in a
new editable workspace.

Scalar substitutions are inserted verbatim: quote them in the template when
needed, for example tool "!.!". A leading @ suppresses the displayed expanded
command but not its output. Environment variables are expanded by the target
shell.

Common substitutions:
  !!       literal exclamation mark
  !.!      current name with extension
  !        current name without the final extension
  !`       extension without the dot
  !~       short name without extension (long-name fallback when unavailable)
  !-!/!+! short name with extension (long-name fallback when unavailable)
  !\ or !/ current panel directory
  !=\ or !=/ resolved real directory
  !:       drive or filesystem root
  !?!      description (currently empty)
  !&       selected names inline
  !&~/Q/q  short names / force quoting / quote only when needed
  !@...!   temporary file containing long selected names
  !$...!   temporary file containing short selected names
  !?title?initial! value requested once before the batch starts
  !# / !^  switch to passive / active panel
  ![ / !]  switch to left / right panel

Active-panel !& and list-file tokens run once for the captured selection.
List modifiers: F full paths, Q quoted entries, S forward slashes, A target
encoding, U UTF-8 with BOM, W UTF-16LE.

@ShellNav
$Panel Navigation Keys
